  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 4.85,
      "end": 11.85,
      "text": "On 275 and 285, also in stereo on VHF, this is National Radio 1.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.85,
      "end": 28.51,
      "text": "Well hello there, Thomas the Vance here, TV on the radio, and welcome once again to the Friday Rock Show.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.51,
      "end": 37.51,
      "text": "This evening, archive sessions by Tyrannosaurus Rex, recorded in 1969 and the early 70s, featuring of course the late and much lamented Mark Bolan.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.51,
      "end": 41.51,
      "text": "We also have a repeat of the first ever session done by Samson.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.51,
      "end": 58.24,
      "text": "We've got some classic cuts by Tommy Bolan, Steve Hackett, UFO, and Santana.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.36,
      "end": 60.66,
      "text": "And new releases by Simple Minds and Jefferson Starship.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.78,
      "end": 62.86,
      "text": "Not a lot of new releases about at this time of the year.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 63.24,
      "end": 67.5,
      "text": "We also have, of course, the answer to the Friday Night Connection we set a fortnight ago.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 67.54,
      "end": 68.16,
      "text": "And a new one.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 70.72,
      "end": 72.84,
      "text": "Tonight we start with ACDC.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 73.74,
      "end": 76.74,
      "text": "The kids are all right.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 721.19,
      "end": 722.31,
      "text": "And the track was Baba O'Reilly.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 722.49,
      "end": 725.05,
      "text": "I played it specially for Derek Dicker, who lives somewhere.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 725.19,
      "end": 728.61,
      "text": "He won't even tell me where, because he scratched out the name of the lighthouse on the front of the car.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 728.61,
      "end": 730.27,
      "text": "I don't know you're out there somewhere, Mr. Dicker.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 730.99,
      "end": 733.91,
      "text": "Also from Sam Walsh of Manchester to his brother Jed,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 733.97,
      "end": 735.71,
      "text": "who's down there in Portsmouth in the Royal Navy.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 736.61,
      "end": 738.31,
      "text": "And I've got a little thing here from Park House,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 738.45,
      "end": 740.87,
      "text": "[redacted address], Mecklesfield in Cheshire.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 741.49,
      "end": 744.71,
      "text": "And it's for Gavin, Leslie and Steve and John and Jim and Dave,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 744.81,
      "end": 745.77,
      "text": "because they wanted to hear the Who.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 746.73,
      "end": 748.95,
      "text": "Before that, you heard High Voltage, ACDC,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 749.09,
      "end": 750.77,
      "text": "from the album If You Want Blood, You've Got It.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 751.17,
      "end": 752.85,
      "text": "That was for Philip Inman and his family,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 753.35,
      "end": 754.75,
      "text": "who live somewhere in the county of Avon.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 755.21,
      "end": 758.85,
      "text": "Also for a load of gentlemen who live in Atlandudno in North Wales.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 758.85,
      "end": 760.81,
      "text": "as Panty Palin, S.A.G.,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 760.81,
      "end": 762.53,
      "text": "Gaz Parallels, Hugh Clark, E. Bish,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 762.61,
      "end": 763.53,
      "text": "Carl Meds and Gwyn,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 763.89,
      "end": 765.73,
      "text": "Carl Kev, Johnny the Knife, Johnst,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 766.13,
      "end": 767.89,
      "text": "Graham, Dave P. and Mark B.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 768.65,
      "end": 771.19,
      "text": "And finally, for a lady by the name of Rebecca Reed,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 771.51,
      "end": 772.43,
      "text": "she lives in Nantwich,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 772.53,
      "end": 773.99,
      "text": "from a gentleman called Dan,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 774.39,
      "end": 775.57,
      "text": "in Crewe in Cheshire.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 778.1,
      "end": 780.12,
      "text": "13 minutes after 10 o'clock, here's Samson.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1409.42,
      "end": 1411.48,
      "text": "Status quo, the greatest boogie band in the world.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1411.6,
      "end": 1413.06,
      "text": "A track from the album Whatever You Want,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1413.12,
      "end": 1414.32,
      "text": "the track was called Breaking Away,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1414.44,
      "end": 1415.62,
      "text": "and that's specially for Scott Millington",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1415.62,
      "end": 1417.34,
      "text": "and Hooligan Smith",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1417.34,
      "end": 1421.6,
      "text": "of Dinnam Hall Ludlow College, because I know they're quo-fans.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1421.88,
      "end": 1426.32,
      "text": "Also, David Wicks, a literate quo-fan, he calls himself here from Leeds,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1426.98,
      "end": 1428.48,
      "text": "which is more than I sound at the moment,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1428.78,
      "end": 1430.74,
      "text": "wanted me to play that track as well, no problem.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1431.18,
      "end": 1434.08,
      "text": "Got a little letter here from Peter Sturratt, I think it is,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1434.1,
      "end": 1437.02,
      "text": "of [redacted address], Salem, Cheshire, who says,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1437.02,
      "end": 1439.1,
      "text": "Dear Tom, what's happened to the Iron Maiden session?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1439.62,
      "end": 1442.9,
      "text": "I'll tell you, Peter, it's going to be played on this programme next week.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1443.24,
      "end": 1446.84,
      "text": "Let's now dig into the archives, go back to May 1969,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1447.34,
      "end": 1452.86,
      "text": "for tyrannosaurus rex",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1452.86,
      "end": 1457.42,
      "text": "many top of the pops fans in europe will have seen or heard our next guests although this is their very first appearance on our show a duo with a style quite unlike",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1457.42,
      "end": 1475.71,
      "text": "that of anyone else in the world they call themselves tyrannosaurus rex",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1781.52,
      "end": 1788.12,
      "text": "Mark Bolan and Steve Took, as they were, in May 1969.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1985.7,
      "end": 1986.54,
      "text": "Tyrannosaurus Rex.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1988.25,
      "end": 1990.93,
      "text": "And the tracks that you heard were Chariot of Silk, Iscariot,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1991.23,
      "end": 1994.39,
      "text": "Once on the Seas of Abyssinia and Misty Coasts of Albany.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1996.46,
      "end": 1999.14,
      "text": "Loads of people asked to hear T-Rex again on the radio,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1999.14,
      "end": 2003.74,
      "text": "and that includes Gary Wilson of Pentalee, I think it is, in Glasgow.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2004.4,
      "end": 2006.76,
      "text": "Also, T. Arkell, good name for a racehorse,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2006.84,
      "end": 2009.46,
      "text": "of [redacted address], New Biggin' by Sea, Northumberland.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2010.08,
      "end": 2011.86,
      "text": "And somebody just called Mark.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2013.06,
      "end": 2016.18,
      "text": "And Aidan D. Brown of Leamington Spa in Warwickshire.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2016.98,
      "end": 2021.86,
      "text": "Cliff McLenahan of Warkington in Kent.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2022.76,
      "end": 2025.32,
      "text": "Oh, we heard this afternoon that the official Mark Boland fan club",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2025.32,
      "end": 2027.12,
      "text": "is going to put out a 12-inch single,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2027.28,
      "end": 2029.16,
      "text": "which is going to include one of the tracks that you just heard,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2029.24,
      "end": 2031.34,
      "text": "the tracks they're going to include on their 12-incher will be",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2031.76,
      "end": 2033.96,
      "text": "Life's a gas, once upon the seas of Abyssinia,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2034.34,
      "end": 2036.84,
      "text": "blessed wild apple girl, and find a little wood.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2037.38,
      "end": 2038.78,
      "text": "If anybody would like to obtain a copy,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2039.26,
      "end": 2040.58,
      "text": "write to the address I'll give you in a second.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2040.68,
      "end": 2042.38,
      "text": "The price of the record is £1.65,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2043.04,
      "end": 2044.44,
      "text": "including postage and packing,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2044.56,
      "end": 2045.9,
      "text": "and the address to get it from is this.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2046.34,
      "end": 2048.3,
      "text": "The official Mark Boland fan club,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2048.98,
      "end": 2050.96,
      "text": "Post Office Box 5,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2051.56,
      "end": 2053.08,
      "text": "Trowbridge in Wiltshire.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2053.5,
      "end": 2055.02,
      "text": "The official Mark Boland fan club,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2055.02,
      "end": 2056.48,
      "text": "Post Office Box 5,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2056.86,
      "end": 2058.12,
      "text": "Trowbridge in Wiltshire.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2058.88,
      "end": 2062.89,
      "text": "And if you didn't catch the address that time around,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2062.97,
      "end": 2064.37,
      "text": "I'll give it to you again later.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2065.09,
      "end": 2072.29,
      "text": "Well, it was three years ago this week that he died, unfortunately.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2853.03,
      "end": 2855.19,
      "text": "Tommy Bolan had a track from his 76 album.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2855.51,
      "end": 2856.83,
      "text": "It was called Private Eyes,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2856.93,
      "end": 2859.55,
      "text": "and that's a real classic from that album, called Post Toasty.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2860.15,
      "end": 2861.21,
      "text": "A load of people remember him.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2861.31,
      "end": 2863.05,
      "text": "We've got cards to prove it in front of us.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2863.11,
      "end": 2864.17,
      "text": "Here's one from Barry Alcock.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2864.27,
      "end": 2867.53,
      "text": "He wants me to say hello to Colin and Tim and Martin and Dave and Andy",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2867.53,
      "end": 2869.29,
      "text": "and definitely wanted a Bolan track.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2869.79,
      "end": 2870.95,
      "text": "I've got a card from Philip Reynolds,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2871.05,
      "end": 2873.49,
      "text": "who wants to be remembered to all his mates",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2873.49,
      "end": 2875.19,
      "text": "at universities and pollies over the country.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2875.63,
      "end": 2879.99,
      "text": "Viz, he says here, Hugh Martin, Gerard Zed, Matt and Jez.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2880.37,
      "end": 2882.91,
      "text": "Little card from a gentleman by the name of Colin Hesketh,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2883.07,
      "end": 2884.23,
      "text": "also calls himself the Teaser.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2884.67,
      "end": 2887.29,
      "text": "He lives in Edenfield, near Bury, in Lanx.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2887.85,
      "end": 2890.75,
      "text": "He says, say howdy to Stephen Mark and Joe Soap and Joe Grimmond",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2890.75,
      "end": 2894.47,
      "text": "and Duke Leopard and Les Howard, Barry Alcock and Ian Steele",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2894.47,
      "end": 2896.07,
      "text": "and all the other bowlingites around the country.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2896.57,
      "end": 2900.05,
      "text": "And finally, a quick mention to Simon Farrant, that is,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2900.05,
      "end": 2902.69,
      "text": "with lots and lots of best wishes from his brother,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2903.25,
      "end": 2904.53,
      "text": "who is called Mark Farrant.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2904.97,
      "end": 2906.35,
      "text": "And the track you heard before that",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2906.35,
      "end": 2909.45,
      "text": "was something from a really ace album that's out on Arista.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2910.17,
      "end": 2912.79,
      "text": "It's called Real to Real Cacophony,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2912.99,
      "end": 2915.37,
      "text": "and it's by a band entitled Simple Minds.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2915.71,
      "end": 2916.99,
      "text": "The track you heard was Changeling.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2917.41,
      "end": 2920.29,
      "text": "And now, here is DC Santana.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2920.89,
      "end": 2925.09,
      "text": "Fabulous session, really good sound on that,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3536.25,
      "end": 3538.49,
      "text": "and tomorrow they're doing their last gig of a tour around the country.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3538.57,
      "end": 3540.93,
      "text": "I'm not absolutely sure where, if I knew I'd tell you,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3540.97,
      "end": 3543.21,
      "text": "but I would invite you to catch them if you can.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3543.27,
      "end": 3545.47,
      "text": "That's Samson, and a track called Take It Like a Man.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3545.55,
      "end": 3547.07,
      "text": "Before that, you heard Carlos Santana",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3547.07,
      "end": 3548.81,
      "text": "from the double album came out in 77.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3549.29,
      "end": 3550.27,
      "text": "It was called Moonflower.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3550.37,
      "end": 3551.29,
      "text": "The track was Europa.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3551.87,
      "end": 3552.83,
      "text": "And that was specially for Claire,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3552.95,
      "end": 3553.79,
      "text": "who's up there in Norwich,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3553.83,
      "end": 3554.89,
      "text": "from Charles, who's at work.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3555.29,
      "end": 3557.47,
      "text": "And also for everybody in the fifth year",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3557.47,
      "end": 3559.19,
      "text": "at Aberdeen Grammar School",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3559.19,
      "end": 3562.47,
      "text": "with very best wishes from David Jack in Aberdeen.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3562.73,
      "end": 3565.71,
      "text": "Now, more out of the archives from 69, T-Rex.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3566.43,
      "end": 3569.43,
      "text": "T-Rex recorded during 1969.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3883.18,
      "end": 3884.92,
      "text": "The tracks he heard were Pavilions of the Sun",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3884.92,
      "end": 3888.12,
      "text": "and First Heart, Mighty Dawn Dart.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3889.88,
      "end": 3891.66,
      "text": "Miss Bowley, he was a really nice fella.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3892.34,
      "end": 3906.06,
      "text": "One and a half minutes after 11 o'clock on the Friday Rock Show,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3906.18,
      "end": 3909.12,
      "text": "now it's time to reveal who's won the Friday Night Connection,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3909.16,
      "end": 3911.08,
      "text": "the one that we set just about a fortnight ago.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3911.24,
      "end": 3912.68,
      "text": "In fact, exactly a fortnight ago.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3913.38,
      "end": 3916.38,
      "text": "I have to tell you here that the winner was £10 better off,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3916.46,
      "end": 3920.98,
      "text": "and he is John Wingfield of [redacted address], St. Leonard's-on-Sea",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3920.98,
      "end": 3922.44,
      "text": "in East Sussex. Well done, John.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3923.56,
      "end": 3926.92,
      "text": "Tracks that we played were Born to Run by Bruce Springsteen,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3927.02,
      "end": 3928.18,
      "text": "whose name I can never get out right,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3928.18,
      "end": 3929.64,
      "text": "Night Moves by Bob Seger,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3930.14,
      "end": 3932.1,
      "text": "and Frankenstein by Edgar Winter.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3933.1,
      "end": 3934.84,
      "text": "And the connection went like this.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3935.32,
      "end": 3937.38,
      "text": "Bruce Springsteen.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3938.86,
      "end": 3939.98,
      "text": "Edgar Winter.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3940.56,
      "end": 3943.38,
      "text": "And if you listened hard to the lyrics of Night Moves,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3943.98,
      "end": 3945.8,
      "text": "you'd hear Summertime in there.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3946.74,
      "end": 3947.26,
      "text": "Seasons.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3948.08,
      "end": 3956.16,
      "text": "The correct answer.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3956.34,
      "end": 3957.58,
      "text": "And John Wingfield, you've got it.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3957.68,
      "end": 3958.58,
      "text": "Congratulations, sir.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3959.45,
      "end": 3963.03,
      "text": "He's also set a mighty tasty Friday night connection of his own.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3963.25,
      "end": 3964.11,
      "text": "You're about to hear it.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3964.11,
      "end": 3966.65,
      "text": "Three bits of music, a definite connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3967.01,
      "end": 3967.23,
      "text": "Listen.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3967.73,
      "end": 3970.73,
      "text": "Friday night connection for tonight,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4758.64,
      "end": 4761.78,
      "text": "put together by John Wingfield of St. Leonard's-on-Sea",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4761.78,
      "end": 4765.64,
      "text": "in East Sussex, and that's a great collection of music.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4770.71,
      "end": 4772.59,
      "text": "And buried in those three pieces of music,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4772.69,
      "end": 4774.45,
      "text": "the titles, the composers, or whatever,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4774.73,
      "end": 4775.91,
      "text": "you will find a connection.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4776.07,
      "end": 4777.19,
      "text": "If you think you know what it is,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4777.25,
      "end": 4778.73,
      "text": "put it down on a postcard in a letter,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4778.89,
      "end": 4780.71,
      "text": "anything you like, any form of communication,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4780.97,
      "end": 4783.27,
      "text": "and send it to the Friday Night Connection,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4783.79,
      "end": 4786.25,
      "text": "the Friday Rock Show, BBC Radio 1,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4786.59,
      "end": 4788.85,
      "text": "London W1A4WW,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4790.18,
      "end": 4791.78,
      "text": "and the one that has the correct answer",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4791.78,
      "end": 4794.7,
      "text": "and the one that we choose will get a £10 record token.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4795.93,
      "end": 4797.65,
      "text": "A little query here from Richard Leonard",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4797.65,
      "end": 4800.37,
      "text": "of [redacted address] in Bridgend, Mid Glamorgan.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4800.53,
      "end": 4802.41,
      "text": "He says, no brief after this week's connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4802.63,
      "end": 4804.83,
      "text": "Whether I win or not, please say whether.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4805.07,
      "end": 4807.85,
      "text": "We have to name the songs as well as the getting the connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4808.35,
      "end": 4810.03,
      "text": "It might save me a lot of 10p's.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4810.41,
      "end": 4811.87,
      "text": "Well, Richard, it's very hard to say.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4811.87,
      "end": 4814.49,
      "text": "In actual fact, no, you don't have to name the songs,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4814.61,
      "end": 4815.65,
      "text": "you don't have to name the LPs,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4815.75,
      "end": 4817.29,
      "text": "all you have to do is get the correct answer.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4817.67,
      "end": 4819.85,
      "text": "But obviously, nine times out of ten,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4819.85,
      "end": 4822.35,
      "text": "it's probably worthwhile you knowing the album they come from",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4822.35,
      "end": 4824.27,
      "text": "and also the name of the song.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4833.34,
      "end": 4836.08,
      "text": "But the right answer will suffice,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4836.4,
      "end": 4838.96,
      "text": "and may I wish you the very best of luck.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4839.44,
      "end": 4842.14,
      "text": "Here's something from a new album by Jefferson Starship.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4842.48,
      "end": 4845.48,
      "text": "Steve Hackett from Spectral Mornings,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5562.86,
      "end": 5564.38,
      "text": "Clocks and Angel of Mon,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5564.48,
      "end": 5566.98,
      "text": "especially for Dick, the number one Genesis,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5567.24,
      "end": 5569.76,
      "text": "and Steve Hackett, Freak, up there in Castleton near Sheffield.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5569.88,
      "end": 5571.82,
      "text": "Also for a load of people,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5572.1,
      "end": 5575.26,
      "text": "they are Chris and Carl and Stephen, Simon and Rick and Andy",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5575.26,
      "end": 5576.9,
      "text": "at school of me and my family.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5577.0,
      "end": 5578.74,
      "text": "I'm referring there to the family of Richard English,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5579.14,
      "end": 5581.96,
      "text": "who lives in Westbury-on-Tyne, I think it is.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5582.06,
      "end": 5585.66,
      "text": "Also, Mr Gary Cousin of Newton Meehan's Glasgow in Scotland",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5585.66,
      "end": 5587.78,
      "text": "is a definite Steve Hackett fan.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5588.26,
      "end": 5590.34,
      "text": "Before that, you heard something from a new album",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5590.34,
      "end": 5591.96,
      "text": "by Jefferson Starship, for my money,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5592.04,
      "end": 5593.34,
      "text": "just about the best one they've ever put out",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5593.34,
      "end": 5594.4,
      "text": "in all the years they've been around.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5594.9,
      "end": 5596.82,
      "text": "The album's called Freedom at Point Zero.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5597.18,
      "end": 5598.06,
      "text": "The track was Awakening,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5598.48,
      "end": 5600.88,
      "text": "and you'll find the album on the Grunt label.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5601.14,
      "end": 5602.6,
      "text": "And now, two from Samson.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6177.05,
      "end": 6178.07,
      "text": "Fabulous session, that was.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6178.07,
      "end": 6179.59,
      "text": "Six Foot Under, the name of the track there,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6179.67,
      "end": 6181.07,
      "text": "and the other track you heard was Big Brother.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6181.19,
      "end": 6182.25,
      "text": "Both of those tracks, incidentally,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6182.31,
      "end": 6184.27,
      "text": "will be found on their LP called Survivors,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6184.35,
      "end": 6186.23,
      "text": "which is out at the moment on Laser Records.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6186.33,
      "end": 6187.27,
      "text": "The name of the band is Samson.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6187.65,
      "end": 6189.37,
      "text": "And somebody very kindly via the phone",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6189.37,
      "end": 6192.53,
      "text": "has told us that Samson are on tomorrow night in Folkestone.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6192.73,
      "end": 6195.07,
      "text": "And our new heavy band session next week",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6195.07,
      "end": 6196.35,
      "text": "is going to be by Iron Maiden.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6197.03,
      "end": 6198.99,
      "text": "OK, let's go back to the early 70s",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6198.99,
      "end": 6202.31,
      "text": "and hear some more delightful stuff from T-Rex.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6203.07,
      "end": 6207.87,
      "text": "X, as they were in the early 70s,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6982.12,
      "end": 6983.48,
      "text": "and there you heard Hot Love.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6983.48,
      "end": 6985.88,
      "text": "It went on to spend six weeks at number one, that record.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6986.14,
      "end": 6988.44,
      "text": "And before that, you heard Jewel, before that, Summertime Blues,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6988.96,
      "end": 6991.1,
      "text": "and before that, By the Light of the Magical Moon.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6991.22,
      "end": 6992.1,
      "text": "Nice to hear that again.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6992.18,
      "end": 6995.2,
      "text": "I'd like to dedicate that, particularly that last track, Hot Love,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6995.32,
      "end": 7000.18,
      "text": "to Colby Hines and Claire, who've just spent 14 months apart,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7000.38,
      "end": 7003.24,
      "text": "and now they're together tonight at the Household Cavalry Hospital.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7003.36,
      "end": 7006.76,
      "text": "They're on the staff, not in the hospital, as patients in Windsor in Barks.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7007.16,
      "end": 7010.06,
      "text": "Next week, our archive session is going to be by UFO,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7010.6,
      "end": 7013.46,
      "text": "which is actually a good name for a band to close on tonight.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7013.48,
      "end": 7013.92,
      "text": "Me thinks.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7014.34,
      "end": 7017.34,
      "text": "...UFO and Shoot Shoot.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7265.08,
      "end": 7266.36,
      "text": "They'll be on the program next week.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7267.22,
      "end": 7269.38,
      "text": "Once again, can I remind you about that address",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7269.38,
      "end": 7271.26,
      "text": "for the official Mark Boland fan club?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7271.34,
      "end": 7272.0,
      "text": "It goes like this.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7272.1,
      "end": 7273.92,
      "text": "Post office box number five,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7274.52,
      "end": 7276.38,
      "text": "Trowbridge in Wiltshire.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7279.38,
      "end": 7280.58,
      "text": "Tomorrow on Rock on a 4 o'clock,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7280.66,
      "end": 7281.98,
      "text": "we're going to be telling you all about our visit",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7281.98,
      "end": 7283.76,
      "text": "to the West Midlands this week",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7283.76,
      "end": 7286.44,
      "text": "to check out the rock scene in Birmingham and Coventry,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7286.54,
      "end": 7287.64,
      "text": "and we're going to meet the Dickies,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7288.0,
      "end": 7289.8,
      "text": "something else you might like to know about tomorrow,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7289.92,
      "end": 7292.32,
      "text": "6.30 in concert, ACDC.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7293.26,
      "end": 7294.8,
      "text": "Our secretary is Susie.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7294.9,
      "end": 7295.44,
      "text": "Thank you, Susie.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7295.52,
      "end": 7297.28,
      "text": "Our engineer tonight was Charles Tarcharles.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7298.16,
      "end": 7300.38,
      "text": "Our producer, as always, is Tony Wilson, who will now speak.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7300.6,
      "end": 7301.2,
      "text": "Good night, all.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7301.28,
      "end": 7302.04,
      "text": "Thank you very much.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7303.28,
      "end": 7304.62,
      "text": "I'll see you tomorrow at 4 o'clock.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7304.72,
      "end": 7306.86,
      "text": "Have yourself a very nice rest of the night.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7307.83,
      "end": 7308.79,
      "text": "God bless and take care.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    }
  ]
}